# Line endings are pinned so this tree can be compared byte-for-byte with the CLI repo.
#
# The docs pages here are MIRRORS: docs/desktop.md is byte-identical to
# windowsweep/docs/desktop.md and is verified with `cmp`. Without this file every
# text type falls to core.autocrlf, which is true on the machines this is edited
# on - so the mirror would become CRLF while its source stayed LF, `cmp` would
# report a difference that is not a difference, and the check the mirror rule
# depends on would quietly stop meaning anything.

* text=auto
*.md text eol=lf
*.mdx text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

# Extensionless, so no rule above reaches them, and each is read line-exact: sh runs the husky hook (a CRLF
# checkout would end its lint-staged line, "--max-arg-length 8000", with a carriage return), nvm reads .nvmrc,
# and prettier checks its own .prettierrc against endOfLine: lf.
.husky/* text eol=lf
.nvmrc text eol=lf
.prettierrc text eol=lf
